CORE
reachable.c
--enforce-contract f _ --pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f\.precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^\[f\.assertion\.1\] .*implementation is reachable: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.
^\s*ASSUME .*r_ok\(f::
--
A function's own contract whose is_fresh size covers the [static N] minimum
satisfies the minimum without assuming the generated requires clause. The
reachability assertion is the only failure, so enforcement is not vacuous.
